      "writtenOn": "2021-04-01T21:58:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "First, I think this line is enough to block the duplicate request.\n\nSecond, RIL/modem should be robust enough. From the HAL definition, there is nothing preventing frameworks to do this. Just like other API setPreferrNetworkMode, if frameworks call 1000 times a second, RIL/modem should treat the rest 999 requests as no-op. This is a very basic design pattern that callee should follow.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 957,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 957,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "de2a939a02b016409ca8673e0cd643e8452f7c0d",
